Objective

The objective of this task is to upload a local project to GitHub and establish a connection between the local Git repository and the remote GitHub repository.

Project Information

Project Name:
Bongo Dev Inventory Management System

Technology:
Node.js, React.js

GitHub Repository:
https://github.com/saifrhmn/bongo-dev-inventory-management-system-by-nodejs-reactjs

Branch:
main

Steps Completed
1. Navigate to the Project

Opened Git Bash and navigated to the local project directory.

cd /path/to/bongo-dev-inventory-management-system-by-nodejs-reactjs
2. Initialize Git Repository

Initialized Git in the local project.

git init
3. Create .gitignore

Created a .gitignore file to prevent unnecessary and sensitive files from being uploaded.

node_modules/
.env
dist/
build/
4. Add Project Files

Added all required project files to Git.

git add .
5. Create Git Commit

Created the initial commit.

git commit -m "Complete TASK 05 - Cloud Connection"
6. Connect Local Repository to GitHub

Added the GitHub repository as the remote repository.

git remote add origin https://github.com/saifrhmn/bongo-dev-inventory-management-system-by-nodejs-reactjs.git
7. Set Main Branch

Changed the local branch name to main.

git branch -M main
8. Push Project to GitHub

Uploaded the project to GitHub.

git push -u origin main
Verification

The project was successfully uploaded to GitHub and is available on the main branch.

